<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/11th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Battle</p><h1 class="enc-title">Battle of Svolder</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1000">1000</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/11th-century">11th century</a> · Also known as Battle of Svoldr</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Battle of Svolder was a naval battle fought in September 1000 in the western Baltic. King <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/olaf-tryggvason">Olaf Tryggvason</a> of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/norway">Norway</a> was defeated and killed by an alliance of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sweyn-forkbeard">Sweyn Forkbeard</a> of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/denmark">Denmark</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/olof-skotkonung">Olof Skötkonung</a> of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sweden">Sweden</a> and Eric Haakonsson, Earl of Lade. The victors divided Norway between them, and the battle became a celebrated subject of the Norse sagas.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/battle-of-svolder.jpg" alt="Battle of Svolder" width="320" height="161" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Otto Sinding · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Svolder,_by_Otto_Sinding.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
<section class="enc-quotes"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Across the Institute</h2><ul><li><blockquote>Kings raised fleets through the leidang, a levy in which coastal districts each equipped and crewed a warship, and the skaldic poems celebrate sea battles such as Hafrsfjord, <b>Svolder</b> in 1000 and Nesjar in 1016, where Olaf Haraldsson defeated Earl Svein Haakonsson.</blockquote><a href="/empire/kingdom-of-norway">Kingdom of Norway · Military</a></li><li><blockquote>…995 with wealth gained as a Viking leader in England and lost it with his life at the <b>Battle of Svolder</b> in 1000, defeated by the kings of Denmark and Sweden and by Eric of Lade, the son of Håkon Jarl, who had been killed as Olaf seized…</blockquote><a href="/societies/vikings">Social Hierarchy of the Vikings</a></li><li><blockquote>After the <b>Battle of Svolder</b> in 1000, his sons Eric and Sweyn governed Norway for the kings of Denmark and Sweden.</blockquote><a href="/state/earldom-of-lade">Earldom of Lade</a></li></ul></section>
